00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:05.749 align:start position:0%
satu motion and leonardo da vinci  devised an ingenious method to find the  area of a circle  partition the circle into slices  split the circle in half and rearrange  corresponding slices to form a  parallelogram-like  shape  if we increase the number of slices and  repeat the entire process  the rearranged shape will approach the  shape of a rectangle  whose width is equal to the radius of  the circle and height is equal to half  the circumference or pi times r  the circle's area  is equal to the rectangle's area  which is r times pi r  and that equals pi r squared  thus the circle's area is pi r squared  incredible
 

